{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1181212-how-do-i-do-an-exorcism-in-mage","id":1181212,"title":"How Do I Do an Exorcism in Mage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-31T13:32:27-08:00","id":1181212,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> How Do I Do an Exorcism in Mage","content":"Dear Sleepers and Awakened (well, maybe not Sleepers),<br /> <br /> In my M20 game this coming Saturday (first Chronicle, second session), the cabal will be approached by Rachel (a friend of a friend) whose husband (Erik) has recently become very unpredictable, with bouts of anger and violence. Upon further investigation, the player characters learn that Erik became possessed by a malevolent spirit when he handled a Native American artifact at the university museum where he works. Rachel and Erik's parents ask the PCs to help since they seem to know what is going on and because they really don't know where else to turn. I want to run this something like the typical horror exorcism plot (The Exorcist, Emily Rose, Vatican Tapes, etc.), and I would like your advice.<br /> <br /> The PCs are just starting out, this is our second session (straight M20 character builds and they got 3 XP the first session).<br /> Here are my questions.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Are PCs with a max of three dots in their spheres capable of handling an exorcism?</li> <li>How do I handle this mechanically, within the M20 rules?</li> <li>Any ideas on how to involve other PCs (6 players total) not directly involved in exorcism?</li> </ol>Thanks in advance - You folks are a wealth of knowledge!!!<br /> <br /> Jim","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23654,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23654-drunkenuraak","user":"DrunkenUraak","date":". 01-31-2018, 05:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23654-drunkenuraak","name":"DrunkenUraak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T14:51:29-08:00","id":1181237,"title":"","content":"M20: How Do You Do That? sets Exorcism as requiring Spirit 4, or dots in the True Faith merit. And while I don't always agree with HDYDT, on this point it seems reasonable. Prime 3 could be used to bribe the possessing spirit with Quintessence, which could either decrease the difficulty of an Exorcism attempt, or be used to entice a spirit to leaving of its own accord. Of course, giving up a mage's own Quintessence - flavored, as it is, with the mage's own spiritual make-up - is potentially dangerous, as it could make it easier for the spirit to possess the mage herself. And bribing without Spirit 4 would require mundane bargaining, and no assurance that it would work, or that the spirit wouldn't go back on its word or try to re-enter the possessed person.<br /> <br /> If your cabal doesn't have anyone with sufficient Arete and/or Sphere knowledge, or True Faith, it might be better to bring in someone else who does. If the PCs have some dots in Spirit, they could collaborate with the NPC to strengthen their Effect.<br /> <br /> Re: How to involve PCs not directly involved in the Exorcism. Keep in mind that while this Exorcism is going on, the spirit itself doesn't need to be idle. Both the Exorcist and spirit can cast other effects on each other (assuming the Exorcist isn't too involved with the ritual to cast other magick, of course, or if the exorcist is an unAwakened person with True Faith). In this case, the spirit is going to use and all spirit Charms it has to disrupt or aggravate the exorcism. The other PCs will likely have their hands full dealing with that nonsense. Levitating objects, visions or illusions, projectile vomiting, called animals, and even spirits summoned by the possessing entity to defend it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T15:33:27-08:00","id":1181247,"title":"","content":"Thank you so much Bluecho for responding. I\u2019m not sure where this HDYDT thing you sited is. I would like to know though. <br /> <br /> Of the group of PCs, one of them has Spirit\u2022\u2022\u2022 and another has Spirit\u2022 plus the True Faith Merit. Additionally, they have a contact which could have a book or other objects to aid their Spiritual needs. With that, I think I could make it work, but it will be challenging for them. <br /> <br /> Of the spirits listed in the M20 book, which would you recommend to use as the possession? Something challenging but doable. Being this is my second M20 session, I\u2019m not too sure about what is challenging yet. Of course, I know I can always tell the story as I desire, but I typically like to keep things as forthright as I can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23654,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23654-drunkenuraak","user":"DrunkenUraak","date":". 01-31-2018, 06:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23654-drunkenuraak","name":"DrunkenUraak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T15:43:14-08:00","id":1181252,"title":"","content":"Spirit 3 allows you to harm spirits. The Spirit being in a body, well you would also need Life 3 to harm the body. True Faith could drive out spirits in a religious ritual like in most movie exorcisms. Also, that character with Spirit 3 could cross over to the other side of the Umbra and find a Spirit with the ability to exorcise the bad spirit. Spirits have a whole hierarchy, so there's problem an opposite number to the evil spirit.<br /> <br /> M20 has a pretty short list of spirits in the main book. I'd look for something more demonic from say, Infernalism: the Path of Screams (Mage: The Sorcerer's Crusade book).<br /> <br /> Other PCs can also be doing research around the location of the exorcism. For example, perhaps they find out what object the spirit broke free from and then make sure to bring it to shove the Spirit back into the original object.<br /> <br /> It's Mage, so while mechanics matter, it's more a game about asserting will than a game with very set spell lists. If an idea is interesting to you and your players and won't do great harm down the road, go with what feels interesting instead of the mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T17:04:27-08:00","id":1181276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrunkenUraak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1181212-how-do-i-do-an-exorcism-in-mage?p=1181247#post1181247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you so much Bluecho for responding. I\u2019m not sure where this HDYDT thing you sited is. I would like to know though.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>How Do You Do That?</i> is a source book released for M20, similar to Book of Secrets and the upcoming <i>Gods, Monsters, And Familiar Strangers</i>. The book talks about how to run various Sphere effects in a mechanical sense, as well as just explains certain mechanics that otherwise couldn't be fit into the main M20 book (like, for instance, Possession). You can find it on Drive Thru RPG.<br /> <br /> While the book and I have a love-hate relationship, some of the material contained therein can be useful. The section on Exorcisms is one of them. If you do get the book, though, take everything you read in it with a grain of salt. The writer, Phil Brucato, loves to overcomplicate aspects of Sphere magick that didn't need such complications, especially in light of previous editions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of the group of PCs, one of them has Spirit\u2022\u2022\u2022 and another has Spirit\u2022 plus the True Faith Merit. Additionally, they have a contact which could have a book or other objects to aid their Spiritual needs. With that, I think I could make it work, but it will be challenging for them. </div> </div> </div>The character with True Faith could do it, though as you've said it might be difficult. It's debatable how other people can help a character running on just True Faith, unless they also happen to have True Faith (and if their faiths happen to be compatible). At least with Spirit, anyone with dots in that Sphere can lend a hand during the casting.<br /> <br /> If the PCs belong to Traditions/Crafts, they could potentially use that organizational structure to call upon a more experienced mage to help them (e.i. one with Spirit 4 or higher, or one with higher True Faith). This might involve the cabal trading favors to the NPC, as bringing a mage out from whatever they were doing previously is a big ask, even if the NPC agrees with the task.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of the spirits listed in the M20 book, which would you recommend to use as the possession? Something challenging but doable. Being this is my second M20 session, I\u2019m not too sure about what is challenging yet. Of course, I know I can always tell the story as I desire, but I typically like to keep things as forthright as I can. </div> </div> </div>I would personally just craft my own spirit for the task, using some of the sample spirits from M20 as a template for stats and Charms. If the players are using beginning characters, it's best to pit them against a minor spirit.<br /> <br /> HDYDT presents the act of Exorcism as being a contested Willpower roll between the spirit and exorcist (both difficulty 8), with each trying to roll a number of successes before their opponent. For the spirit, they need to roll successes equal to the exorcist's Willpower + Avatar, plus 2 successes for each dot in True Faith (if applicable). The exorcist, meanwhile, needs to roll enough to match the &quot;general power&quot; of the spirit, says the book. It lists a graduating number based on overall potency, with minor spirits requiring 10 successes, and going up from there. Since the PCs are just starting out, making the spirit &quot;minor&quot; is a good idea, unless the characters bring in a particularly potent NPC to help (in which case, increase the success threshold appropriately to the NPC's ability).<br /> <br /> As for spirit Charms, the spirit can have any powers suitable for its nature, or you can make up whatever ones you like for dramatic purposes. If it makes for an interesting exorcism scene - and isn't too great for the beginning characters to handle - throw it in. If it's a minor spirit, it will probably only have one or two such Charms it can employ (in addition to the Possession Charm needed to even be here). And it'll only be able to use those Charms so many times before it depletes its supply of Essence, so look at the sample spirits for an appropriate Essence score. This turns the exorcism into a battle of attrition as much as wills.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T17:19:48-08:00","id":1181282,"title":"","content":"One more thing: Since one of the PCs has True Faith, the spirit should probably be of a nature that makes it an ideological enemy of that character. While any malevolent spirit will likely make it appropriately anathema to most characters with True Faith - a spirit that does wrong by people will tend to be opposed by most characters who are not themselves evil (like an Infernalist or Nephandi with a dark True Faith) - making the spirit be of a worldview that is consistent with the PC's faith will help make the game internally consistent. At least to start. You can venture into &quot;stranger&quot; types of spirits later, as the characters get more familiar with the wider world. Keeping it consistent now will cut down on complications in the immediate sense, as well as help validate the player's choices in character creation.<br /> <br /> If the cabal ends up getting an NPC mage or True Faith exorcist to help, it might be more appropriate to match the spirit to them, instead. As if to say that the characters are bringing in a specialist to help. It ultimately depends on how the players go about preparing for the exorcism, and what their characters end up doing. If the players lean on doing the rite themselves, make the spirit appropriate to them. If they decide to get help, make it appropriate to the NPC, if there's a qualitative difference (if it's the True Faith PC that's calling for help, the NPC will likely be of the same cultural tradition anyway).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T03:12:41-08:00","id":1181353,"title":"","content":"Womble Spoon it. The possession came from handling a Native American item, so get that involved. Maybe it's a Wonder in it's own right that can help but working out how to use it will require some leg work and the skills of the cabal, or maybe using it with Correspondence + Spirit holds the answer. There's a whole host of possibilities that may not require Spirit 4. <br /> <br /> I find when I'm running Mage it helps to have a rough idea of the 'plot thing' and a few ideas on exactly how to approach dealing with it, then listen to you players and what they think might work as they are investigating things, if they have good ideas that you like then let that shape the solution. Also make note of their Paradigms, it's possible that a given characters understanding of The Way the Universe Really Works may open up options that others may not see (and a player may not realize because they don't have your story notes).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T04:42:05-08:00","id":1181618,"title":"","content":"I'd also wager that any Shaman or Spirittalker worth their salt would just do that at first - talk to the Spirit in question and essentially ask 'What's up?'. Even without Spirit 4, often enough a spirit can be coaxed out of the body. even if not, at least the Shaman can learn what the spirit *wants*, and maybe get it done without actually getting into direct conflict with the thing.<br /> <br /> On the other hand if you have a Templar mage, you're going to get from 0 to exorcism in no-time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":".  Typos! 02-02-2018, 07:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-11T16:07:44-08:00","id":1184936,"title":"","content":"As said further up, Spirit:3 can allow you to harm the spirit; it can also allow you to attempt to lull it, which while not directly exorcising it (which would require Spirit:4, reversing the channeling concept that also exists at that level) can at least mitigate its current influence until a more permanent solution can be reached. (In the DA:M setting, Dreamspeakers/Spirit Talkers have a metaphysical edge in that regard: they can use either Wise One:3 (and a contested WP roll with the spirit/entity in question, though with a bonus equal to the successes above 1 than they rolled added to their WP) or Chieftan: 4 to directly compel the spirit (the DS/ST's successes being directly measured, uncontested, against the appropriate power-stat; if sufficient are rolled, the spirit is ejected).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T10:59:05-08:00","id":1192668,"title":"","content":"I will phrase this as a joke, but please take into account that this is a true possibility, which is even included in the Dreamspeekers Rev. Edition: you can always use Spirit 2 to beat the shit out of the spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6470-sardonis","name":"Sardonis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T05:19:39-08:00","id":1193058,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you can. Spirit 2 allows to touch the Umbra, so you can beat the shit out of a ghost until it leaves by free will. Assuming the ghost isn't a masochistic specter/Bane that likes it, it may work. It doesn't allow to beat a possessing spirit w/o beating the host, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T13:35:20-08:00","id":1193290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1181212-how-do-i-do-an-exorcism-in-mage?p=1193058#post1193058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, you can. Spirit 2 allows to touch the Umbra, so you can beat the shit out of a ghost until it leaves by free will. Assuming the ghost isn't a masochistic specter/Bane that likes it, it may work. It doesn't allow to beat a possessing spirit w/o beating the host, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>As such, unless you want to <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=H4A1haySbx8\" target=\"_blank\">make like the Boondocks</a>, you'll need a bit more than just Spirit 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T05:55:38-08:00","id":1193498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As such, unless you want to <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=H4A1haySbx8\" target=\"_blank\">make like the Boondocks</a>, you'll need a bit more than just Spirit 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey!, beating the crap out of the possesed it's <i>very </i>Traditional.<br /> <br /> It IS suggested in the Dreamspeaker Tradition Book. There's a Rote built arround that idea and all.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T07:39:03-08:00","id":1193547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sardonis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1181212-how-do-i-do-an-exorcism-in-mage?p=1192668#post1192668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will phrase this as a joke, but please take into account that this is a true possibility, which is even included in the Dreamspeekers Rev. Edition: you can always use Spirit 2 to beat the shit out of the spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good point, but ST, please keep the Agency of your ghost/demon/bane in mind.<br /> <br /> If you were possessing a mortal and some weird magic-user started beating the shit out of you, you would try and respond in kind. Threaten to damage the body you've possessed, or use some ability you have.<br /> <br /> For example, if a PC were trying to exorcise a Bane from a mortal, then they would start vomiting acid all over the person who was trying to stop them. If the spirit is a Demon, suddenly our Exorcist finds that the ceiling is their reference point for gravity and they fall upwards, distracting them too much to continue. Make escape their main priority, ideally with the body they've possessed, but not necessarily. And if they chase you out, there isn't much they can do to stop you from coming back. Just wait it out and possess them again, maybe be more subtle about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T07:40:34-08:00","id":1193548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1181212-how-do-i-do-an-exorcism-in-mage?p=1181618#post1181618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also wager that any Shaman or Spirittalker worth their salt would just do that at first - talk to the Spirit in question and essentially ask 'What's up?'. Even without Spirit 4, often enough a spirit can be coaxed out of the body. even if not, at least the Shaman can learn what the spirit *wants*, and maybe get it done without actually getting into direct conflict with the thing.<br /> <br /> On the other hand if you have a Templar mage, you're going to get from 0 to exorcism in no-time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking with Native American Wraith: &quot;So you just wanted to find out what happened to your husband's remains? Listen, if you step out of their body I can make myself a Fetter and take you down to city hall, we can look through records and see what happened. Okay?&quot;<br /> <br /> Templar: &quot;BEGONE FOUL SHADE!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 03-09-2018, 10:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T23:56:20-08:00","id":1193832,"title":"","content":"What about curses? I know you use Entropy to curse people, and I assume you can use Entropy to lift curses. But what if you don't know Entropy. Is there any other combination of spheres that would work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T00:12:14-08:00","id":1193834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1181212-how-do-i-do-an-exorcism-in-mage?p=1193547#post1193547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a good point, but ST, please keep the Agency of your ghost/demon/bane in mind.<br /> <br /> If you were possessing a mortal and some weird magic-user started beating the shit out of you, you would try and respond in kind. Threaten to damage the body you've possessed, or use some ability you have.<br /> <br /> For example, if a PC were trying to exorcise a Bane from a mortal, then they would start vomiting acid all over the person who was trying to stop them. If the spirit is a Demon, suddenly our Exorcist finds that the ceiling is their reference point for gravity and they fall upwards, distracting them too much to continue. Make escape their main priority, ideally with the body they've possessed, but not necessarily. And if they chase you out, there isn't much they can do to stop you from coming back. Just wait it out and possess them again, maybe be more subtle about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bare in mind a Mage can do a hell of alot more than just Punch and the spirit isn't going to know until they've had shit cast on them that its not just some random mortal holy guy trying to waste their time(and even the punches could be &quot;Akashic demon smashing PUNCH!&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T20:16:25-07:00","id":1194427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1181212-how-do-i-do-an-exorcism-in-mage?p=1193058#post1193058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, you can. Spirit 2 allows to touch the Umbra, so you can beat the shit out of a ghost until it leaves by free will. Assuming the ghost isn't a masochistic specter/Bane that likes it, it may work. It doesn't allow to beat a possessing spirit w/o beating the host, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, there's a reason those Pentecostal exorcisms are so rough on the kids undergoing them!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T06:21:48-07:00","id":1194506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1181212-how-do-i-do-an-exorcism-in-mage?p=1193832#post1193832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about curses? I know you use Entropy to curse people, and I assume you can use Entropy to lift curses. But what if you don't know Entropy. Is there any other combination of spheres that would work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Prime, to erase it's supernatural foundation.<br /> <br /> Depending on the nature of the curse other Spheres could work too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T00:01:53-07:00","id":1194752,"title":"","content":"I wonder if you could use an older understanding of Correspondence (Connection from <i>The Sorcerer's Crusade</i>) to sever the link between the curse and its target without technically nullifying it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T03:05:10-07:00","id":1194778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1181212-how-do-i-do-an-exorcism-in-mage?p=1194752#post1194752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if you could use an older understanding of Correspondence (Connection from <i>The Sorcerer's Crusade</i>) to sever the link between the curse and its target without technically nullifying it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if HDYDT is to be believed, Correspondence can't do squat on its own and pretty much just functions as an adjunct to 'real' spheres. Then again HDYDT is awful and I'm pretty sure Brucatto has no idea how Mage chargen works and what sphere levels are realistic in a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T07:32:08-07:00","id":1194832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1181212-how-do-i-do-an-exorcism-in-mage?p=1194778#post1194778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if HDYDT is to be believed, Correspondence can't do squat on its own and pretty much just functions as an adjunct to 'real' spheres. Then again HDYDT is awful and I'm pretty sure Brucatto has no idea how Mage chargen works and what sphere levels are realistic in a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, HDYDT and Mage Core state that, for example, teleporting whole patterns, transposing locations, creating portals, grasping whole patterns etc. works purely on Correspondence alone.<br /> Relocating *parts* of a pattern, teleporting things out of patterns, casting effects remotely and ripping chunks out of the landscape needs correspondence combined with othere spheres.<br /> <br /> The only conflicting entry regarding this are the actual Correspondence 2/3 sphere descriptions, but I think this has just fallen victim to 'must mention other spheres with every entry' habit, since the Correspondence main paragraph goes into quite some detail regarding the 'whole pattern teleportation' thing not needing any other spheres.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 03-13-2018, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T09:48:12-07:00","id":1194873,"title":"","content":"My main beef is that wards, arguably the main function of Correspondence, have completely insane requirements in HDYDT and do require conjunction spheres for basically everything from what is being warded to what is being warded against. The example of warding a computer against men in black is Correspondence 4/Forces 3/Life 4/Matter 4/Mind 4/Prime 2. And you can generously expand it to warding against all living things by removing Mind 4. That's 17 Sphere dots to stop people from touching your computer. Come on.<br /> <br /> The guidelines on Correspondence are contradictory. &quot;Common Magical Effects&quot; puts Teleport on Correspondence 3 (4). Meanwhile, the <i>description</i> of Correspondence 3 says:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, by combining Correspondence 3 with Forces, Life, or Matter, the mage can move things around from a distance, levitating, manipulating or teleporting them without physical contact. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12892,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","user":"Kammerer","date":". 03-14-2018, 04:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T21:56:47-07:00","id":1195128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1181212-how-do-i-do-an-exorcism-in-mage?p=1194873#post1194873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My main beef is that wards, arguably the main function of Correspondence, have completely insane requirements in HDYDT and do require conjunction spheres for basically everything from what is being warded to what is being warded against. The example of warding computer against men in black is Correspondence 4/Forces 3/Life 4/Matter 4/Mind 4/Prime 2. And you can generously expand it to warding against all living things by removing Mind 4. That's 17 Sphere dots to stop people from touching your computer. Come on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeeeeeeah, pretty much. I so won't argue against HDYDT being a cherry-picker of a book because of things like that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I think that's common, ahem, consensus here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T01:14:37-07:00","id":1195177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1181212-how-do-i-do-an-exorcism-in-mage?p=1194873#post1194873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The guidelines on Correspondence are contradictory. &quot;Common Magical Effects&quot; puts Teleport on Correspondence 3 (4). Meanwhile, the <i>description</i> of Correspondence 3 says:</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, yep, that's what I meant in regards to the Correspondence Sphere Level writeup.<br /> Peek at the pre-Sphere-Levels text of Correspondence. it goes into quite some detail about how Correspondence alone is enough for whole patterns, and explicitely states that working on parts of patterns (the example goes for teleporting/displacing somebody's head) would need Life. With how much words are spend on that, I tend to go with that instead of the short blurbs in the levels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T06:29:09-07:00","id":1195257,"title":"","content":"Yeah, as I have stated numerous times: M20 has many lovely rules about magick, but did a terrible job explaining how Spheres work. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins Fan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if you could use an older understanding of Correspondence (Connection from <i>The Sorcerer's Crusade</i>) to sever the link between the curse and its target without technically nullifying it?</div> </div> </div> </div>However, M20 does state that in order to counter a spell you don't always need to have all of the Spheres used in it's casting. Sometimes the whole spell it's dependant on a Sphere as a medium/vector and canceling it it's enough to stop the magick. And the example it's Correspondence. You can stop ranged spells by closing the Correspondence channel.<br /> <br /> It stands to reason that curses can be ended (or temporarily ended) in a similar fashion, but only in cases where the source of the Curse is acting at distance. If the curse is locked on the Pattern of the afflicted person then it won't work (you would need a much more complex, reasonably multi-sphere, effect to sepparate the curse from the victim)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T13:28:43-07:00","id":1195448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1181212-how-do-i-do-an-exorcism-in-mage?p=1195257#post1195257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, as I have stated numerous times: M20 has many lovely rules about magick, but did a terrible job explaining how Spheres work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, I stick with my interpretation drawn from a mishmash of 2E, Sorcerer's Crusade, and Revised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T10:23:49-07:00","id":1195778,"title":"","content":"All excellent ways.<br /> You can always confine the possessed victim and use the combined spirit spheres to contact good aligned spirits to intervene and force it out to be manipulated or bound into a bottle of sand. From this safe point it can be questioned and perhaps appeased..<br /> <br /> Or just thrown into a weighted chest which in turn is dropped into the ocean.<br /> <br /> (Magic the Gathering Deck Black/White Deck quote. Blessed be that Treachery!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23973-silentline","user":"Silentline","date":". 03-15-2018, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23973-silentline","name":"Silentline","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T05:30:04-07:00","id":1196018,"title":"","content":"Is there any way to bounce the curse back onto the caster? Something plus correspondence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T07:09:22-07:00","id":1196039,"title":"","content":"There's two potential ways.<br /> <br /> *Offensive Countermagick lets you bounce spells back (albeit it's not easy), but it's rules aren't applicable after the spell was casted - that's Unweaving territory.<br /> <br /> *If you have the same Spheres used to cast the curse at distance, nothing impedes you from not only cleanse the curse but also send it back trough the same Correspondence chanel.<br /> <br /> RAW you can't change the target (nor any property) of a spell after it has been casted without casting it again (and getting more sucesses). The only exception it's Unweaving/Countermagic (thus Unweaving the connection of a spell seems viable to me, but changing it's target doesn't)<br /> <br /> As a hack, I would allow to toy with the idea of creating some sort of countermagical material/barrier, like Primium, but that acts like Offensive Countermagick. That would allow to create a &quot;spell mirror&quot; of sorts. But it would be very high level stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}